# Public values only. Every name starts with EXPO_PUBLIC_, and Expo inlines it into the app bundle,
# so anyone with the app can read it. Secrets never go in the app: keep them on a server.
#
# Real values live in EAS environment variables (`eas env:create`) for builds, and in a local
# .env (git-ignored) for development. Copy this file to .env and fill it in.
# Each variable here is also read in src/env.ts, the only module that reads process.env.
#
# Example:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
